infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title 100 RPS vs 1,000,000 RPS are different systems
  desc The order of magnitude from stage 2 decides which components are even legal in stage 3
  compares
    - label 100 RPS · a few GB
      children
        - label One Postgres instance
          desc The correct, simplest answer
        - label One app server
          desc No fleet needed
        - label No sharding
          desc Partitioning here is over-engineering
        - label No message queue
          desc Async would be premature
    - label 1,000,000 RPS
      children
        - label Partitioning
          desc Single store is a non-starter
        - label Caching tiers
          desc From the first sketch
        - label Async processing
          desc Queues become mandatory
        - label A fleet, not a box
          desc 10,000x the load
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
